# The odor decoder. What is committed is what the generator (step 2) and the classifier (step 3) start from, and
# the PubChem cache; everything else is made again by ds-prepare and ds-build:
#   ds-prepare  data/raw/pyrfume-data/        the odor sources, from a pinned commit
#   ds-build    data/raw/pubchem/CID-*         the PubChem download (1.5 GB + 1.3 GB, 14 GB unpacked)
#               data/processed/odor/*          the tables, the packed tokens and the PubChem intermediates
# Committed: the vocabulary (the token numbers a saved model is tied to), the fine-tuning table, the cache of
# PubChem answers (so a rerun needs no network), and the pretrained decoder (23 MB). The pretraining inputs
# (structures.csv, 674 MB, and the packed tokens, 201 MB) are over GitHub's 100 MB limit and are rebuilt.
data/raw/pyrfume-data/
data/raw/pubchem/*
!data/raw/pubchem/odor_pubchem.csv
data/processed/odor/*
!data/processed/odor/vocabulary.json
!data/processed/odor/odor_dataset.csv
data/processed/odor_dev/

# Trained models and the logs of their runs, except the pretrained decoder that steps 2 and 3 read
output/*
!output/odor/
output/odor/*
!output/odor/stage1/
output/odor/stage1/*
!output/odor/stage1/best.pt
*.part
